 "description": "Kestrel Bay Port and Freight Authority is an invented regional Australian statutory authority that operates wharves, container and bulk terminals, freight yards, pilot and tug bases, and a logistics park. It manages berth booking, pilotage, dangerous-goods permits, port security and freight coordination across a dispersed coastal network, working with shipping lines, rail operators, transport companies and primary producers. The authority runs safety, environmental and trade-facilitation programmes, publishes port notices, and maintains a head office with corporate, engineering and harbour-master functions. All names, identifiers and contact details in this profile are fictional and institutional only.",
